Practical: lowercase, then replace every char that is NOT letter-or-digit-or-whitespace using a check function instead of regex charclass:

```js
function normalizeClaim(text) {
   var s = String(text || '').toLowerCase();
   var out = [];
   for (var i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {
       var c = s.charAt(i);
       if (/[a-z0-9\s]/.test(c) || c.charCodeAt(0) > 127) out.push(c);
       else out.push(' ');
